# gen_fu_shape_check: every shape the manifests declare as a stimulus gap, at every seed

WHAT THIS CLAIMS. Two runs of one checker over 40 seeds each. The RED run reads the generators
committed at 8559958805f7c942f9c2feeafe87aec03a7118a3 and fails; the GREEN run reads the same two
generators with this touch's edits and passes. Both runs read their targets from the SAME two
manifests, which this touch does not modify, so the runs differ in the generators alone. This is
a MODEL-LEVEL claim about the instruction shapes the programs emit, not a claim that any bin is
hit. The bins themselves are settled by simulation in the companion retained log
gen_fu_generator_fix_sweep.log, where both entries hit every declared bin at all forty seeds.

